<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piyale Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1515–1578</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piyale Pasha was an Ottoman admiral (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapudan-pasha">Kapudan Pasha</a>) under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and Selim II, of Croatian or Hungarian origin. He defeated a Spanish-led fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djerba">Djerba</a> in 1560, commanded the fleet at the unsuccessful siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> in 1565, and took Chios from the Genoese without a fight in 1566. He married a daughter of Selim II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piyale-pasha.jpg" alt="Piyale Pasha" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VikiPicture · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piyale_Pasha_bust_at_Istanbul_Naval_Museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
